From 1a7d31d650a01085a68e72567134f298ae879707 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "xiu.yang" <xiu.yang@sophgo.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:12:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(cvsnfc): read GD5F2GM7 in 4-bit mode to speed up rootfs
 cold reads

[description ]:
- drivers/mtd/nand/raw/cvitek/cvsnfc_spi_ids.c: set
  FLAGS_SUPPORT_4BIT_READ on the GD5F2GM7UEYIG entry.
- spi_nand_read_from_cache() already selects the read command from this
  flag: with the flag it issues 0x6B (READ FROM CACHE x4), without it
  it falls back to 0x0B (x2). Only the chip table entry was missing.
- BF01 rootfs is squashfs on UBI over this SPI NAND, so every cold read
  of busybox, the inittab and the init scripts pays this cost.

[root   cause]:
- The GD5F2GM7UEYIG entry carried .flags = 0, so the driver always took
  the x2 branch even though the QE bit is enabled at probe ("Enabling QE
  bit for GD5F2GM7UEYIG"). QE only permits quad transfers, it does not
  change the read opcode.
- At the 93MHz SCK inherited from U-Boot, a 2KB page takes ~88us on two
  lines and ~44us on four, which halves the transfer part of every page
  read.

[JIRA      ID]:TBD-BF01-BOOTTIME
[chip project]:181x
[side effects]:
- Affects only boards using the GD5F2GM7UEYIG; other chip entries are
  unchanged and keep their current mode.
- Verified on cv1815ja_bf01_spinand: raw /dev/mtd read 9.7 -> 12.9MB/s,
  Run /sbin/init -> preinit: enter 380 -> 158ms on the same slot.
- No uncorrectable ECC, no "retry read", mtd ecc_failures stays 0 across
  repeated boots.
- The remaining ~115us per page is fixed overhead (tR, DMA setup, ECC
  status read), so expect ~1.3x, not 2x.

[Affected *.ko/*.so/*.a] :none (source-only change; cvsnfc is built-in)

Change-Id: I1c79c3f8df4002e19e85be3e7b5d0351c8fc5c44
---
 drivers/mtd/nand/raw/cvitek/cvsnfc_spi_ids.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/cvitek/cvsnfc_spi_ids.c b/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/cvitek/cvsnfc_spi_ids.c
index 2adcf3276945aebb5e1f50b3fa6fb5f632bb7110..ed819a1b97860138fa392cf6ed6b343ee68af18b 100644
--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/cvitek/cvsnfc_spi_ids.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/cvitek/cvsnfc_spi_ids.c
@@ -1092,7 +1092,7 @@ struct cvsnfc_chip_info nand_flash_cvitek_supported_ids[] = {
 			.length = 0,
 			.locked = 0,
 		},
-		.flags = 0
+		.flags = FLAGS_SUPPORT_4BIT_READ
 	},
 
 	{
